---
slug: test/mcp-client-metadata
format: json
---
{%- comment -%}
  TEST FIXTURE (gated): a Client ID Metadata Document served by the test instance
  itself, so tests/oauth.test.mjs can drive commands/oauth/resolve_client through a
  real fetch. Its client_id is this page's own URL, as CIMD requires. The client name
  holds a real quote and HTML entities: the document must be parsed without decoding
  them. Served only when MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS is '1'/'true' (CI + eval hosts).

  The JSON is written as literal text: platformOS encodes a hash with & < > as
  & < >, but other servers (JSON.stringify, for one) send them as is,
  and only literal entities show whether the parser decodes them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign test_gate = context.constants.MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS | default: ''
  if test_gate == '1' or test_gate == 'true'
    function origin = 'modules/mcp/queries/origin'
    assign doc = '{"client_id":"' | append: origin | append: '/test/mcp-client-metadata.json","client_name":"CIMD \"q\" &quot;e&quot; &amp; &lt;b&gt;","redirect_uris":["https://client-cimd.example.test/cb"],"token_endpoint_auth_method":"none"}'
    print doc
  else
    response_status 404
    echo '{}'
  endif
-%}
